/* DISCOVERY / derivation (CONTRIBUTION 3): the ADAPTIVE information-exploration duality -- the rigorous
   SEQUENTIAL upgrade of results 10 (static Cramer-Rao) and 11 (static Av+B/v rule). At round t the
   controller injects exploration variance v_t; the accumulated Fisher information about the effect is
   I_t = m0 + sum_{s<=t} v_s/sigma^2 (each round adds v_s/sigma^2, m0 the prior/van-Trees info). The
   VAN TREES (Bayesian Cramer-Rao) inequality bounds the Bayes risk of the effect estimate BELOW by
   1/I_t even for SEQUENTIAL/adaptive observations (ordinary CR does not apply to adaptive designs), so
   the per-round estimation regret is >= C/I_t. Any schedule pays cumulative regret >= sum_t [A*v_t +
   C/I_t]. Minimising it gives a DECREASING optimal schedule that stops once the information threshold is
   reached -- not the static single v* of result 11. Maxima is the source of truth. */
display2d : false$

/* per-round tradeoff at accumulated info level m (=I before this round, in variance units): exploration
   cost A*v plus the van-Trees estimation floor K/(m+v), K = C*sigma^2. */
f(v) := A*v + K/(m + v)$
print("per-round tradeoff f(v) = A*v + K/(m+v),  A = b^2+rr,  K = C*sigma^2 (van-Trees floor numerator)")$

/* optimal single-round exploration: f'(v) = A - K/(m+v)^2 = 0 => (m+v*)^2 = K/A => v* = sqrt(K/A) - m */
fp : diff(f(v), v)$
vstar : rhs(solve(fp = 0, v)[2])$
print("f'(v) =", fp, " ; optimal v* =", vstar, " = sqrt(K/A) - m")$
print("f''(v) =", ratsimp(diff(f(v), v, 2)), " > 0 : convex, v* the unique interior optimum")$

/* the SOS optimality identity (sqrt-free via (m+vs)^2 = K/A): f(v) - f(v*) = A*(v - v*)^2/(m+v) >= 0 */
gap : ratsimp( (A*v + (A*vs^2)/(m + v)) - (A*vs + (A*vs^2)/(m + vs)) )$   /* K replaced by A*(m+vs)^2, and m+vs=... */
print("f(v)-f(v*) SOS check: A*(v-vs)^2/(m+v) - gap_form =",
      ratsimp(A*(v - vs)^2/(m + v) - ((A*v + A*(m+vs)^2/(m+v)) - (A*vs + A*(m+vs)^2/(m+vs)))),
      " (0 confirms f(v)-f(v*) = A*(v-vs)^2/(m+v))")$

/* THE SCHEDULE: at round t the accumulated info is m_t (increasing in t), and the optimal increment is
   v_t* = max(0, sqrt(K/A) - m_t). Since m_t increases, v_t* DECREASES, and hits 0 once
   m_t >= sqrt(K/A) -- the information THRESHOLD after which exploration is no longer optimal. */
print("optimal schedule v_t* = max(0, sqrt(K/A) - m_t) : DECREASING in t (m_t increases)")$
print("stops when m_t >= sqrt(K/A) : the information threshold (learned enough)")$
print("=> a DECREASING schedule, not the static single v* of result 11")$

/* van Trees floor is ANTITONE in accumulated info: more exploration so far => lower estimation floor. */
print("van-Trees floor K/(m0 + I) is antitone in accumulated info I (Rocq: van_trees_floor_antitone)")$

/* contrast with result 11 (static): result 11 minimises A*v + B/v (single-shot, m=0), giving a CONSTANT
   v* applied every round -- which OVER-explores (keeps paying A*v after info is plentiful). The adaptive
   schedule strictly improves cumulative regret by tapering exploration to the van-Trees floor. */
print("static (result 11) v*=sqrt(B/A) applied every round over-explores; adaptive schedule tapers")$
